WEBVTT

00:21:56.913 --> 00:22:01.829
and it was really nerve wracking. It took
an entire year to get a full time job.

00:22:02.288 --> 00:22:06.829
In 2001, Emily had just graduated with her
bachelor's degree in psychology when

00:22:06.829 --> 00:22:10.329
she lived through her first of three
recessions, the dotcom bust.

00:22:10.621 --> 00:22:12.996
During the boom of the late 90s,

00:22:13.246 --> 00:22:17.329
there was just an incredible sense
of entitlement of what's

00:22:17.329 --> 00:22:21.413
the world going to offer me? Should
I start my own company?

00:22:21.413 --> 00:22:26.079
Will I be a millionaire? By twenty
five expectations that were insane.

00:22:26.829 --> 00:22:29.496
And you fast forward two
years to my class

00:22:29.496 --> 00:22:32.413
and it just it had completely changed.